  "reading": {
   "title": "Turkey or America?",
   "text": "Hafsa and Linda are talking about life in the United States and life in Turkey.\n\n\"Is life here more expensive than in Isparta?\" Linda asks. \"Yes, it is,\" says Hafsa. \"Rent is much higher here. But salaries are better, too. My cousin in Isparta works longer hours and earns less.\"\n\n\"What about the traffic?\" Linda asks. Hafsa laughs. \"Isparta is smaller and quieter, so the traffic is lighter. Here the roads are bigger, but they are busier. The bus at five o'clock is the most crowded place in the city!\"\n\n\"Which do you like better?\" Linda asks. Hafsa thinks. \"My house in Isparta was more comfortable, but my new job here is more interesting. Emre says this is the best place for his future. I think he is right.\"",
